Note that this advice is for mid-game play.  If you can make it to
Gehennom you probably don't need (want?) the advice.  On special levels
the rules are going to be all different anyhow.  This is for plowing
through the dungeon to rack up XP and stuff.

Back to the stash list:
Stash:
Spellbooks! (weigh a lot)
Backup armor except one cloak
Backup tools
Backup weapons except daggers
most unlabelled scrolls (all if you don't have a marker)
extra markers
uncursed water and potions that aren't useful in battle
most food
duplicates of most rings
all rings/amulets for which you already have the intrinsic (you better
have poison resistance by now)
Most zorkmids
gems except a few hard gems
Any other junk that is valuable but the RNG seems to be particularly
generous with today
valuable polymorph fodder
any un'ID'd stuff
backup and non-combat wands (e.g. polymorph, create monster)

Keep in bag:
some Food (or one Horn of Plenty)
backup ammo
1-2 holy water
1-2 potions of [foo] healing
Backup cloak
a couple combat wands, undead turning to save your pet, maybe secret
door detection
Pickaxe! (if you aren't using it as a weapon) weighs a ton
other tools if not in use (esp. unicorn horn if not used as weapon)
couple more combat scrolls
some zorkmids (not a lot)
a few gems including one hard one
marker and a couple of blank scrolls

Open inventory:
Daggers/ammo (you can't use that many unless you are an Expert)
rings/amulets you may want in melee
one or 2 wands you may want in melee
one or 2 scrolls you may want in melee (e.g. teleportation, scare
monster)
1 holy water (to uncurse the bag or your 2-handed weapon if you get a
malignant aura)
lizard corpse
luckstone
blindfold/towel
tools in active use (e.g. stethoscope, key, magic whistle)
a small amount of gold

Wear/wield:
Primary armor
Primary weapon
(optional, level dependent) reflection, searching, warning, ESP,
protection, slow digestion, telecontrol, polycontrol, ...

I keep zorkmids around to bribe demons and to keep leprechauns engaged
rather than running away.  You don't need many.  Also if you find a
shop at a deep level, you probably only want a few things that are in
it, so you can just buy them rather than hassle with stealing or
killing; we can spare the inventory for the modest amount of gold it
takes to buy most things.



